course: dictionary
lesson: 6633
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Novel is a noun and an adjective. As a noun, a novel is a long story in a book about made-up people and events. «The class novel is about a girl who finds a secret door.» The clue is class: it is a book you read over many lessons.
explain: As an adjective, novel means new, different and interesting. «Her novel idea was to paint the classroom walls black.» Idea is a thing, and novel describes it. Ask yourself: is this word naming something, or describing something? The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: Check by swapping the meaning into the sentence. If «a new idea» still makes sense, the adjective meaning is right. If «a long story in a book» fits better, it is the noun.
fact: A novel (noun) is a long story in a book about made-up people and events.
fact: Novel (adjective) means new, different and interesting, as in «a novel solution».
fact: Graphic novels are books where the story is told with words and pictures together.
fact: «Journey to the West» is a novel that turned the real trip of the monk Xuanzang into an adventure with the Monkey King.
fact: In «Les Misérables», Jean Valjean is sent to prison for years for stealing a loaf of bread to feed his sister's hungry children.
exercise: «The class novel is about a girl who finds a secret door.» What is a novel here? | A type of pencil case | A short poem | *A long story in a book about made-up people | A new, unusual idea
exercise: «Her novel solution to the problem surprised everyone.» What does novel mean here? | Very old | A kind of story | Long and boring | *New and different
exercise: Graphic novels are real reading. How do you work out the story? | Only by looking at the pictures, with no words | *From the words and the pictures together | By reading the last page first | By skipping every page
test: In «a novel idea», what does novel mean? | A long book | Ancient | *New, different and interesting | Very sad
test: In «the novel Les Misérables», what does novel mean? | New and different | A kind of prison | Very old | *A long story in a book about made-up people and events
exam: Which sentence uses novel as an adjective? | *«Her novel idea made the whole class laugh.» | «Comics and graphic novels are on the shelf.» | «The class novel has three hundred pages.» | «The novel was read aloud every Friday.»
